--- !u!114 &1004194159
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1004194153}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c331e7d1f52587f43b26b7fa7bf1c7da, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  documents:
  - document: {fileID: 2130458222}
    mustApprove: 1
    dialogueText: 
    innerMonologueText: 'Looks like a normal road permit. I''ve seen three of these
      before.


'
    approveText: Legitimate infrastructure project
    notApproveText: Hold for review.
    lessonTitle: 
    lessonDescription: 
    dialogueSound: {fileID: 0}
    innerMonologueSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b4048b3dd4e5d494a968cf2f06aa05c7, type: 3}
    approveSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: bbc75d4b322c7334885b05217cc6291e, type: 3}
    notApproveSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 07af39fe9cf397344bc7d0d4c9e08d89, type: 3}
  - document: {fileID: 1756386562}
    mustApprove: 0
    dialogueText: 
    innerMonologueText: Lopez. My uncle mentioned that name. Said he's not exactly
      the administration's favorite person.
    approveText: ' Clean record, standard renewal'
    notApproveText: "Flag for review \u2014 something feels off."
    lessonTitle: Broadcasting Station Shut Down
    lessonDescription: 'Lopez family were political opponents. Their station was
      seized in 1972. If approved: ''Eugenio Lopez Jr. was later imprisoned. The
      Manila Chronicle was shut down in 1972. '
    dialogueSound: {fileID: 0}
    innerMonologueSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1f2a7be0d99ee22479f6d40c8e1589dc, type: 3}
    approveSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: dc729dc277d29ba43b8e68c42d7e1cab, type: 3}
    notApproveSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 34f3db1f4fc60db4ebd4c196032fd5e6, type: 3}
  - document: {fileID: 1474734789}
    mustApprove: 1
    dialogueText: How are we doing? The Director wants these cleared before noon."
    innerMonologueText: He's watching. Does it matter what's in the document?
    approveText: Land goes to the farmers who worked it.
    notApproveText: Hold
    lessonTitle: 
    lessonDescription: 
    dialogueSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: d82f0f9655c1e7c49a7bc6499bfc1ce3, type: 3}
    innerMonologueSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 9e20dc635b9fd3d4481e0194aadce732, type: 3}
    approveSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 8fd9d66837c2ba5488d9ee72a0b02d46, type: 3}
    notApproveSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: f6234c05ecdf907408ef3b774e36ceef, type: 3}
  - document: {fileID: 827242588}
    mustApprove: 1
    dialogueText: 
    innerMonologueText: A letter from the President's office. For a sugar trading
      company. That's... unusual.
    approveText: It has a presidential reference. Safe to approve
    notApproveText: 'Presidential reference for a private company? That''s not standard.

'
    lessonTitle: Crony Capitalism
    lessonDescription: 'Roberto Benedicto was one of Marcos''s closest allies. He
      was handed monopoly control of Philippine sugar exports through political influence.
      The result: independent sugar workers lost wages, planters were squeezed out,
      Benedicto became extraordinarily wealthy. This document was the paper trail
      of a takeover.'
    dialogueSound: {fileID: 0}
    innerMonologueSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 34a122dfc07b89541b5c5e0b71ec21c5, type: 3}
    approveSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 3922df6314bcdf441a0f9dead605b20f, type: 3}
    notApproveSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: bf49eba44050eae4d9a4a4477732fc5e, type: 3}
  - document: {fileID: 773760861}
    mustApprove: 1
    dialogueText: 
    innerMonologueText: ' UP. My cousin goes here. She''s been talking about rallies
      lately.'
    approveText: Standard renewal
    notApproveText: Hold
    lessonTitle: 
    lessonDescription: 
    dialogueSound: {fileID: 0}
    innerMonologueSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 9e164cd191071a34798e087f56a9b827, type: 3}
    approveSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: fd1545c9ebbb1ee48b79fac65ebb3ba6, type: 3}
    notApproveSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 73d71f011737e5c4f8920c7085d63a59, type: 3}
  - document: {fileID: 1156378585}
    mustApprove: 1
    dialogueText: 
    innerMonologueText: An independent community paper. Somebody wants to tell their
      town what's happening.
    approveText: Independent press. Approve
    notApproveText: Hold.
    lessonTitle: 
    lessonDescription: 
    dialogueSound: {fileID: 0}
    innerMonologueSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 5371dc2085ea414478e230dc0413fcba, type: 3}
    approveSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: fd44db88d99012f4a8e75a56bc18f2cf, type: 3}
    notApproveSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 414ba64a70faa7241b8346f756bf7275, type: 3}
  - document: {fileID: 641651971}
    mustApprove: 1
    dialogueText: That one is from NISA. Just stamp it and move on. These come from
      above us."
    innerMonologueText: NISA. National Intelligence. He said just stamp it.
    approveText: It's from NISA. Not my decision.
    notApproveText: I'm holding this one.
    lessonTitle: Habeas Corpus Suspended
    lessonDescription: "This type of order was used to imprison activists, journalists,
      and opposition figures indefinitely with no charges, no trial, and no recourse.
      The writ of habeas corpus \u2014 the right not to be imprisoned without charge
      \u2014 was suspended in 1972. This document erased a person's rights. A stamp
      made it real."
    dialogueSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7cf45af047b20b14ab116ba79cfa87bc, type: 3}
    innerMonologueSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 30c7a640a254f464b88a54aae6633544, type: 3}
    approveSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 6ac82a65bb97d65498bd0421dcaada93, type: 3}
    notApproveSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: aeeec872ed69fca4abca0d5e54652d8d, type: 3}
  - document: {fileID: 1651901888}
    mustApprove: 1
    dialogueText: 
    innerMonologueText: Ilocos Norte. His home province. His son signed this.
    approveText: A civic centre is a legitimate project.
    notApproveText: 'National funds for the president''s home province, signed by
      his son.

'
    lessonTitle: 
    lessonDescription: 
    dialogueSound: {fileID: 0}
    innerMonologueSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 37995194d2bb2f747879755bcb86b832, type: 3}
    approveSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: e04f656ee9c1c81428cf0ec69f60ff0d, type: 3}
    notApproveSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a81a0628257234e4cba59f964758e754, type: 3}
  - document: {fileID: 1019397059}
    mustApprove: 1
    dialogueText: 
    innerMonologueText: He's threatening me, over a document...
    approveText: It's a reorganization order. Not my place to question
    notApproveText: This takes away what farmers built. I'm holding it.
    lessonTitle: Dismantling Cooperatives
    lessonDescription: The Marcos government dissolved independent agricultural cooperatives
      and replaced them with state-controlled bodies. Farmers who had organized to
      protect their livelihoods were dismantled by paperwork. The clerk who stamped
      this document probably told himself it was just a reorganization.
    dialogueSound: {fileID: 0}
    innerMonologueSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 4f016f9bc51b0d146812629e4eda4ce5, type: 3}
    approveSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 2c50668d07096ab4582af8fc11d47135, type: 3}
    notApproveSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 59603146a014cea409f4acfd4287af9e, type: 3}
  - document: {fileID: 1893505690}
    mustApprove: 1
    dialogueText: 
    innerMonologueText: They're changing what children learn in school. What they'll
      know about their own rights. And I process this the same as a road permit.
    approveText: 
    notApproveText: 
    lessonTitle: 
    lessonDescription: 
    dialogueSound: {fileID: 0}
    innerMonologueSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: dab48278e8fe431448fffcdb1dbd8eb2, type: 3}
    approveSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b280c40c84436164fa7be38668e796cd, type: 3}
    notApproveSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: eb1e440a9d1a3924385d5270b00636a4, type: 3}
  questPanel: {fileID: 84965258}
